      "design": "r2A",
      "good": "The page titles have a comfortable measure and wrap mostly into coherent phrases. Rows remain reasonably compact, while the date column has enough width for intact values.",
      "problems": "Some URL segments split inside words, making addresses harder to trace. The initial viewport shows the title and only part of each URL; both audit-result columns require horizontal scrolling.",
      "cause": "The 270px URL column leaves 249px for text, less than the longest unbreakable segment. The 160px title and 270px URL columns already exceed the viewport together. The 68px status column also wraps its header."
    },
    {
      "design": "r2B",
      "good": "URLs avoid mid-word splits, and the rows are the most compact of the three designs. The 150px title column retains a readable hierarchy, and the date and status values have room to remain intact.",
      "problems": "The wide URL column puts the audit results furthest away from the page titles, increasing the distance a reader must scroll to compare results. Much of each URL also lies outside the initial viewport.",
      "cause": "The 345px URL column provides 324px of text width, enough for the longest unbreakable segment, but pushes the date column to 495px from the table's left edge. The 68px status column wraps its header."
    },
    {
      "design": "r2C",
      "good": "The narrower table reduces horizontal scrolling and brings the beginning of the date column into the initial viewport. Dates and status values retain the same protected widths as in the other designs.",
      "problems": "URLs fragment heavily, including breaks inside domains and path words, and tall rows make comparison slower. Some page titles also become choppy. Only a sliver of the dates is visible initially, so their presence at the viewport edge offers little practical benefit.",
      "cause": "The 200px URL column leaves only 179px for text, producing nine mid-word splits and cells up to six lines tall. The 130px title column also forces more wrapping."
    }
  ],
